IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nt-part8-transitional`

-- Tests of nt-part8-transitional.l4 (sections 73 to 78).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the section named beside it.

§ `Sections 73 and 74`

#ASSERT `s 73: the reference to regulations is taken to include a reference to rules or by-laws` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 73: the reference to regulations is taken to include a reference to rules or by-laws` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 73: the reference to regulations is taken to include a reference to rules or by-laws` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The example under section 74: Regulations No. 5 of 2005 may be cited as Subordinate Legislation No. 5 of 2005.
#ASSERT `s 74: the citation of the subordinate legislation by its number and year` TRUE 5 2005 EQUALS JUST "Subordinate Legislation No. 5 of 2005"
#ASSERT `s 74: the citation of the subordinate legislation by its number and year` TRUE 12 2003 EQUALS JUST "Subordinate Legislation No. 12 of 2003"
#ASSERT `s 74: the citation of the subordinate legislation by its number and year` FALSE 5 2005 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 75 and 76`

#ASSERT `s 75(1)(a), (b), (c): the short title or reference is taken to include the year of enactment or making` `the short title of an Act that, but for section 4(1) of the Amendments Incorporation Act 1938, would have included the year of enactment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75(1)(a), (b), (c): the short title or reference is taken to include the year of enactment or making` `the short title of subordinate legislation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75(1)(a), (b), (c): the short title or reference is taken to include the year of enactment or making` `a reference in an Act or subordinate legislation to another Act or subordinate legislation by its short title` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Before the repeal, the text gives no such effect.
#ASSERT `s 75(1)(a), (b), (c): the short title or reference is taken to include the year of enactment or making` `the short title of subordinate legislation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 75(1)(a), (b), (c): the short title or reference is taken to include the year of enactment or making` `some other short title or reference` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 75(1)(d): the short title including the year may be substituted for another form of reference` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75(1)(d): the short title including the year may be substituted for another form of reference` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 75(2): the reference in the other document fails` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 75(2): the reference in the other document fails` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76: section 50(1) applies to the reference` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76: section 50(1) applies to the reference` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The example under section 76.
#ASSERT `s 76, example: the reference to the Local Court Act 2015 is a reference to it as amended from time to time` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76, example: the reference to the Local Court Act 2015 is a reference to it as amended from time to time` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Sections 77 and 78`

#ASSERT `s 77: the order is taken to have been made under section 35 as in force after the commencement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 77: the order is taken to have been made under section 35 as in force after the commencement` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 78: the former section 63 continues until the 12 sitting days expire (taken here to be 20 June 2022).
#ASSERT `s 78: section 63 as formerly in force continues to apply to the subordinate legislation on the day` `regulations made before the commencement` (Date 20 6 2022) (Date 20 6 2022) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 78: section 63 as formerly in force continues to apply to the subordinate legislation on the day` `regulations made before the commencement` (Date 20 6 2022) (Date 21 6 2022) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 78: section 63 as formerly in force continues to apply to the subordinate legislation on the day` `rules or by-laws signed under section 63(2)(a) before the commencement` (Date 20 6 2022) (Date 19 6 2022) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 78: section 63 as formerly in force continues to apply to the subordinate legislation on the day` `rules or by-laws signed under section 63(2)(a) before the commencement` (Date 20 6 2022) (Date 21 6 2022) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 78: section 63 as formerly in force continues to apply to the subordinate legislation on the day` `other subordinate legislation` (Date 20 6 2022) (Date 19 6 2022) EQUALS NOTHING
